{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6715116","formula":"C₂₁H₂₃N₃O₂","hill":"C21H23N3O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":23.0,"N":3.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"MDA-19"},"descriptions":{"en":"MDA-19 (also known as BZO-HEXOXIZID) is a drug that acts as a potent and selective agonist for the cannabinoid receptor CB2, with reasonable selectivity over the psychoactive CB1 receptor, though with some variation between species. In animal studies it was effective for the treatment of neuropathic pain, but did not affect rat locomotor activity in that specific study. The pharmacology of MDA-19 in rat cannabinoid receptors have been demonstrated to function differently than human cannabinoid receptors with MDA-19 binding to human CB1 receptors 6.9× higher than rat CB1 receptors."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":25034599,"mass":349.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCCN1C2=CC=CC=C2/C(=N/NC(=O)C3=CC=CC=C3)/C1=O","inchikey":"ZGQHMZCITJHYOW-QOCHGBHMSA-N","iupac":"N-[(Z)-(1-hexyl-2-oxoindol-3-ylidene)amino]benzamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"25034599","atoms":49,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.368,"y":0.724,"z":0.644,"el":"O"},{"x":4.224,"y":-1.593,"z":-0.841,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.637,"y":-0.553,"z":0.696,"el":"N"},{"x":1.529,"y":-1.7,"z":-0.349,"el":"N"},{"x":2.259,"y":-0.572,"z":-0.166,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.426,"y":1.026,"z":0.076,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.617,"y":0.374,"z":1.193,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.453,"y":2.032,"z":0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.93,"y":-1.891,"z":0.353,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.204,"y":2.711,"z":-0.541,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.784,"y":-2.545,"z":-0.098,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.292,"y":-0.279,"z":0.485,"el":"C"},{"x":0.289,"y":-1.572,"z":-0.037,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.224,"y":3.75,"z":-0.069,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.14,"y":-2.557,"z":0.417,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.782,"y":-3.864,"z":-0.5,"el":"C"},{"x":